* DONE [#B] <<initiateSub Command>> Add =initiateSub= command            :ai:
CLOSED: [2026-07-14 Mon] SCHEDULED: <2026-07-14 Mon>
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:07
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 6 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
Requires =--activity= (no inheritance from parent). Preconditions:
1. Walk up from target directory looking for a =CLAUDE.md= symlink whose
   target lands under the configured =templatesBase=. If none, refuse.
2. Target directory must not already have a =CLAUDE.md=. If it does, refuse.
Install: slim =CLAUDE.md= (symlink to =mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md=),
=AI-Activity.org= (symlink), =AI-DevStatus.org= and =AI-WorkPlan.org=
(safe-copy with dblock expansion). Does NOT install 
=AI-WORKFLOW.org=, or =.claude/=.
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented in =py3/bin/aiActivity.cs=. New template at
=mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md= imports only =@./AI-Activity.org=,
=@./AI-DevStatus.org=, =@./AI-WorkPlan.org=. Precondition uses symlink-
target check (readlink + relative_to templatesBase) — no content parsing.
Nested =initiateSub= works because both base and sub CLAUDE.md symlinks
land under =templatesBase=, so the precondition treats them equivalently.
End-to-end verified: refusal on isolated dir, refusal when CLAUDE.md
already present, success in properly-nested child, success in
grandchild (nested case).

