=aiSuspend= should NOT unlink =CLAUDE.md= — it should rename it to
=CLAUDE.md.dormant=, preserving the symlink target as the mode signature.
=aiResume= should read =CLAUDE.md.dormant='s target: if it points at
=mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md=, restore in sub mode (no 
=AI-WORKFLOW.org=, or =.claude/=); otherwise base mode.
----- AI Results: ------
=aiSuspend= now stashes CLAUDE.md → CLAUDE.md.dormant instead of removing
it. The other symlinks (=AI-WORKFLOW.org=, =AI-Activity.org=)
are still removed since they can be re-derived. =aiResume= reads the
=.dormant= symlink target, compares against
=<templatesBase>/mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md= (resolved), sets
=subMode= boolean, and gates the AI-WORKFLOW/.claude/ install
blocks on it. If no =CLAUDE.md.dormant= is found, defaults to base mode.
Verified: base-mode suspend/resume cycle unchanged from Stage 4;
sub-mode cycle correctly restores the slim overlay without touching
inherited invariants. =deClaudify= updated to also remove =.dormant=
files (base and sub), in case cleanup runs while suspended.

