dir — expect =EH_Problem_UsageError= refusal). Uses =lpDo= for
uniform logging.
----- AI Results: ------
Wrote =py3/test/verify.sh=. Shebang =#!/bin/bash -i= (needed so
=~/.bashrc= runs its interactive body and defines =_opDo=; =lpDo= is
an alias defined there and needs =bash -i= to expand). Uses
=lpDo eval rm -rf ... 2\>/dev/null= for silent cleanup (escaped
redirect so eval sees it as shell syntax). Uses =lpDo pushd= / =popd=
around the =/tmp= negative case for visible directory changes, and
=lpDo eval rm -rf "$TMPDIR"= to clean up. Full cycle exits 0 and
leaves the test directory containing only =verify.sh= itself.
Refusal is visible in the trace as
=EH_Problem_UsageError: No initiated parent found for /tmp/tmp.*=.

