* DONE [#A] <<CLAUDE.md Safe-Copy>> Switch CLAUDE.md from symlink to safe-copy in initiate/initiateSub :ai:
CLOSED: [2026-07-17 Wed] SCHEDULED: <2026-07-17 Wed>
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:12
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 11 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
=initiate= and =initiateSub= now =shutil.copy2= =CLAUDE.md= from
=mother/CLAUDE.md= (base) or =mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md= (sub)
instead of symlinking. No provenance line for =CLAUDE.md= --- must be
byte-identical to the template. =deClaudify= moved =CLAUDE.md= (and
=CLAUDE.md.dormant=) from the symlink-only list to the removable-files
list so it removes either form. =aiSuspend= now =rename=-s =CLAUDE.md=
→ =CLAUDE.md.dormant= (file, not symlink); if a legacy symlink is
found, it is unlinked. =aiResume= promotes =CLAUDE.md.dormant= back
if present, or re-copies from templates.
----- AI Results: ------
Mode detection needed to change: previously =aiResume= and =initiateSub=
compared the =CLAUDE.md= symlink target against
=<templatesBase>/mother/initiateSub/CLAUDE.md= to distinguish sub from
base. Since =CLAUDE.md= is now a copy, both switched to walking up for
a parent =AI-WORKFLOW.org= symlink under =templatesBase=. =AI-WORKFLOW.org=
remains a symlink (harmless --- it has no =@./= back-imports), so this
signature is still available. =initiateSub= precondition and =aiResume=
mode-detection both use the same walk-up helper logic (inlined for now;
extract to a helper if a third caller emerges).

