----- AI Results: ------

Discussed the Open items from =AI-Outputs.org='s "Process Design" section
(now removed from that file --- content consolidated here) and closed each:

- *Destination*: confirmed as an extra symlink hop, not a new repo.
  =mother/AI-Outputs.org= is itself a symlink into a separate blee-binders
  repo (=blee-binders/evolution/aiActivity-outputs/=, renamed from
  =aiActivity-evolution= --- the original name read as "the evolution of
  the aiActivity tool," when the binder actually holds outputs generated
  *through* aiActivity, not about aiActivity itself). This resolves the
  original concern (don't make =mother/= a high-churn write target)
  without inventing new repo machinery in =bisos.aiActivity= --- the tool
  only ever creates one symlink, identical in shape to =AI-WORKFLOW.org=.
  =bxexamples/aiActivityTemplates= is deliberately NOT given this symlink
  now; it will get a real (non-symlinked) file later, with a note that
  BISOS's symlink approach is optional to mirror.
- *In the import chain or not*: decided NOT imported by =CLAUDE.md=.
  Read via =/bx-ai-outputs= (index mode) or opened directly when relevant.
- *Growth*: not a blocking design problem --- an operating-discipline
  matter (drain the =TODO=/=WORKAROUND= backlog regularly).
- *=/bx-ai-outputs= command*: written at
  =mother/_claude/commands/bx-ai-outputs.md=. No argument = index mode,
  grouped =WORKAROUND= first then =TODO= then =INFO=, read-only. An
  argument = capture mode --- drafts an entry (asks for keyword and
  =:REPO:= if unclear, since the fix-repo is often not the current repo),
  shows it for confirmation, then appends under the matching existing
  top-level section (or a new one). Not the only way to write --- the file
  is an ordinary symlinked org file --- but keeps entries consistent.
- *Dangling symlinks*: accepted as a known, pre-existing risk class
  (same as =AI-WORKFLOW.org='s own repo dependency). No action needed.

=bisos.aiActivity= engine changes (=py3/bin/aiActivity.cs=), all following
the existing =AI-WORKFLOW.org= symlink pattern exactly, and all treating
=AI-Outputs.org= as optional (skip silently if the templates tree doesn't
ship it, e.g. =bxexamples= / the fork today):

- =initiate=: installs the =AI-Outputs.org= symlink from =mother/=.
- =initiateSub=: unchanged by design --- inherits from the parent, exactly
  like =AI-WORKFLOW.org=, rather than installing its own copy.
- =aiSuspend= / =deClaudify=: remove the symlink.
- =aiResume=: reinstalls it, base mode only.
- =refresh=: extended to *backfill* the symlink when missing --- this is
  the retroactive path for already-=initiate=-d projects that predate this
  feature, reusing =refresh= rather than adding a new command. Verified in
  an isolated directory: =MODE: base= → =SYMLINKED (backfilled)=.
- =py3/tests/verify.sh=: extended with coverage for install / remove /
  reinstall / backfill. Full harness run passes (exit 0). One pre-existing
  quirk surfaced during testing, unrelated to this change: running the
  harness from =py3/tests/= --- nested inside this repo's own self-=
  initiate=-d tree --- causes =aiResume=/=refresh= to always detect "sub"
  mode, because the walk-up finds the *parent* aiActivity project's own
  =AI-WORKFLOW.org= symlink even when the target directory has its own
  genuine base install. Pre-existing (same walk-up code path used for
  =AI-WORKFLOW.org= before this stage), not introduced here, and out of
  scope for this stage --- logged as a Stage 14 candidate.
- Documented the =TODO=/=WORKAROUND=/=INFO= keyword vocabulary and the
  =:REPO:= convention in =AI-WORKFLOW.org= (new "AI-Outputs.org ---
  Cross-Project Findings Ledger" section), plus a new table row and a
  =/bx-ai-outputs= row in the slash-commands table.

