=_resolveTemplatesBaseSub= gives a sub a valid templates base when none is
given: CLI, cwdConfig, *nearest* initiated ancestor, userConfig, auto-detect.
Used by =initiateSub=, =refresh= and the =examples= menu; base =initiate= is
unchanged ("only applies to sub").
- Deviation from the TODO: the ancestor is the *nearest* with an
  =AI-WORKFLOW.org= symlink into a templates tree, read from that symlink, not
  the top-most ancestor's =.aiActivity.cs= config. Nearest is the right one
  when trees nest; homogeneous is the default.
- Heterogeneous is explicit and honoured: =--templates= or cwdConfig naming
  another tree gives a =HETEROGENEOUS= note, not a refusal (an earlier version
  refused it, contradicting the README topology section).
- Verified in scratch dirs (userConfig pointing at a fork): homogeneous sub
  follows its parent; heterogeneous sub installs from the explicit tree. The
  =examples= change was only compile-checked. =verify.sh= has both cases but
  was not run in full.

