:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
Consider the ones mentioned in [[Stage 16]]
Discuss the concept and decide on the right name.
----- Results: ------

Name decided: *=startupClaudeTokens=* (module =startupClaudeTokens_csu.py=).
=aiStatus= rejected (too close to =/bx-status=); =aiInTokens= was the runner-up.
First chosen as =startupTokens=, then renamed (same day) after a discussion of
Claude specificity: the command encodes only Claude Code's loading rules, so a
generic name would overclaim. It is part of the /Claude binding/, alongside
=listClaudesPath= and =deClaudify= (see the design decision in =AI-DevStatus.org=).

Concept: a static estimate of the tokens Claude Code loads *at session
start* from a given cwd, broken down by source, so the human can reshape
the chain (archive, move into a subdir, trim an =AI-Activity.org=) before
paying for it. Not telemetry --- no runtime observation.

Design decisions (agreed), each correcting the =aiStatusOutine.py= outline:
- *Follow =@= imports* recursively instead of counting a fixed 5-file
  list. The bulk of the cost is in imports (=bisos-pip/AI-Activity.org=
  pulls in ~6 panels).
- *Separate "startup" from "on demand".* Subdirectory =CLAUDE.md= files
  below cwd load only when Claude touches that subtree --- listed
  separately, not summed into the startup total.
- *Include all startup sources*: managed policy, user =~/.claude/=, the
  walk-up chain, rules, auto-memory =MEMORY.md=, skill/command descriptions.
  System prompt + tool definitions mentioned as fixed overhead, not measured.
- *Drop the cache-status section.* Prompt caching is server-side and
  prefix-keyed; file mtimes say nothing about it.
- chars/4 estimate, labelled as such.

Claude Code loading rules verified against the official memory/skills docs
(code.claude.com/docs/en/memory.md, skills.md) on 2026-10-07:
- Walk-up goes from cwd to the *filesystem root*, not the git root;
  =CLAUDE.local.md= appended after =CLAUDE.md= at each level.
  (=listClaudesPath= stops at git root --- a divergence, noted for Stage 14.)
- =@= imports: anywhere in a line, relative to the importing file, =~=
  supported, max 4 hops, skipped inside markdown code spans / fenced blocks.
- Auto-memory =MEMORY.md=: first 200 lines or 25KB.
- Skills: only frontmatter description (+ =when_to_use=, capped 1,536
  chars) at startup; discovered from cwd up to the repo root.
- Unconfirmed in docs: whether =.claude/commands/*.md= descriptions load at
  startup (treated like skills).

* DONE [#A] <<16.4>> Add /bx-context-trim --- in-session counterpart of startupClaudeTokens
CLOSED: [2026-10-07 Wed] SCHEDULED: <2026-10-07 Wed>
:PROPERTIES:
