This is all towards simplifying user experience. To not show the user what is not relevant.
- At the root of a git repo, with no args: show only the =initiate= section;
  the =initiateSub= section has just =aiActivity.cs -i examples=.
- In a git repo but not at its root, with no args: show only the
  =initiateSub= section; the =initiate= section has just =aiActivity.cs -i examples=.
- =aiActivity.cs -i examples=: show both, as before.
- Outside any git repo, with no args: show both, and above the =initiate= and
  =initiateSub= sections say that there is no repo.
- Whether or not the directory is already initiated, the rule above applies;
  mark the activity that is here (from the =AI-Activity.org= symlink, else
  cwdConfig).
- The "Based on CWD Setting" section follows the same rule.
- Where =initiateSub= is shown but no initiated parent exists, say so.
----- Results: ------

Implemented in the =examples= cmnd of =py3/bin/aiActivity.cs= (body after
=####+END:=, no dblock touched), with two new helpers, =_gitRepoRoot()= and
=_activityHere()=.
- Bare vs =-i examples=: both run the same class (=noCmndEntry=examples=), but
  =cs.G.icmRunArgsGet().invokes= is =None= on a bare run and =['examples']=
  otherwise. Testing =invokes= (not argv length) keeps =aiActivity.cs -v 30=
  a bare run.
- Repo root: =git rev-parse --show-toplevel=, so a nested repo or submodule
  is its own root. =listClaudesPath= still has its own copy; fold it into
  =_gitRepoRoot()= with [[14.10]].
- Marker: =<== activity here= on the matching =initiate= / =initiateSub= line.
- Verified by hand (repo root, =py3/=, =py3/images/= sub, outside a repo, a
  fresh repo with no initiated parent, =-i examples=, =-v 30=) and by new
  =verify.sh= cases; =verify.sh= ran clean on 2026-10-09.
- Not done: the Blee panel and README don't describe the context menu yet.

