----- Results: ------
----- AI Results: ------
Design drafted 2026-10-19 (no code written), after reading =aiActivity.cs= (templates resolution,
=initiate=, =refresh=, =commonParamsSpecify=), =startupClaudeTokens_csu.py= and =verify.sh=, and loading
=writing-cs-commands=, =comeega-authorship=, =dblock-authoring=, =bisos-pip-setup-py=. Not marked DONE:
awaiting review.

*Files* (all under =py3/=; =setup.py= is regenerated by =pypiProc.sh=, which picks up a new =bin/*.cs=):
- =bin/aiActivityCmnds.cs= --- a =cs-mu= csxu, empty =csuList=, its own =examples= (=noCli=) menu.
- =bisos/aiActivity/cmndsSync.py= --- the logic as pure functions (=pyLibPure=, =pathlib= only, no =cs=
  import), so =verify.sh= and a scratch run can exercise it without the framework. The =.cs= holds only
  parameters, =Cmnd= classes and reporting. (Not a =_csu.py=: =aiActivityCmnds.cs= is its own
  command, not a
  unit imported by =aiActivity.cs=.)
- =README.org=: a section "aiActivityCmnds.cs --- a template-maintainer tool". No Blee-panel edit (dblock
  regeneration, in Blee).

*Commands* (verbs, the PyCS way, in place of flags):
| =cmndsDiff=  | read-only: what a sync would add, update, delete; exit 0                     |
| =cmndsCheck= | one line, =IN SYNC= or =BEHIND= with counts (exit-code caveat below)         |
| =cmndsSync=  | applies it; =--prune= also deletes target =.md= files absent from the source |

*Parameters*: the source tree defaults to =/bisos/apps/defaults/ai-templates= when it exists; the
target is
*mandatory and has no default*, because a sync deletes (with =--prune=) and a wrong default would be
destructive. The names =--from= / =--to= you proposed cannot be Python keyword arguments (=from=), so the
=parName= would be =fromTemplates= / =toTemplates=, with =argparseLongOpt= =--from= / =--to=: to be
tried in
[[17.4]]; fall back to =--fromTemplates= / =--toTemplates= if the framework ties the argparse name to the
keyword.

*Behaviour*
- Scope: =<tree>/mother/_claude/commands/*.md= only. Never =settings.json=, never skills, never
  =activity/_claude=.
- Copies are byte-identical (no header edit). /Correction to my earlier proposal/: a Claude Code command
  file without frontmatter takes its first line as the description shown in the slash menu, so a
  prepended
  "do not edit" line would replace every description. The marker goes in a sidecar, =.syncedFrom= in the
  target =commands/= directory: source tree, its git commit if it has one, the date, and a sha256
  per file.
  A dot-file is meant to be ignored by Claude Code: [[17.4]] verifies it does not appear as a command.
- Without =--prune=, extras in the target are reported and kept (safe for a locally added command).
  With it,
  they are deleted after being listed. The first sync into the fork needs =--prune=, since the
  five old
  names are in no manifest.
- =cmndsCheck= counts an extra as drift, since the target is meant to equal the source.
- Refuses (nothing written): source or target missing; target has no =mother/_claude/commands=; the two
  resolve to the same directory; the target's =commands= is a symlink. A source of bxexamples is fine; a
  target of bxexamples is not refused by the tool (hand-maintained is a convention, not enforced)
  --- say so, or add a refusal, in [[17.4]].
- Never commits; after a run it prints the target's =git status --short= for
  =mother/_claude/commands= when
  the target is in a repository, so the review is one step.

*Caveat*: the =bx-pals-web-site= skill notes that the PyCS main exits 0 even when a =Cmnd= fails. So
=cmndsCheck= may not be able to give a non-zero exit. With the hook dropped ([[17.1]]), this only costs a
shell-script use of =--check=; confirm in [[17.4]] and, if so, say it in the README rather than
work around
the framework.

*Test plan for [[17.4]]*: scratch source and target trees under =mktemp -d= (as =verify.sh= already
does for
the no-parent case), a section appended to =verify.sh=: target with two old names and one shared file;
=cmndsDiff=, =cmndsCheck= (BEHIND); =cmndsSync= without =--prune= (extras kept); with =--prune=;
=cmndsCheck= (IN SYNC); second run idempotent; the four refusals; =settings.json= byte-unchanged;
=.syncedFrom= not offered as a slash command in a real session.

*Found for [[17.5]]* (read there, not changed): =initiate= prefers =<activity>/_claude/commands= over
=mother/_claude/commands= when it exists. No activity has one today (=ls */_claude=: =mother= only). "No
layering for commands" suggests dropping that override for =commands= (keeping it for =settings.json=):
decide in 17.5.


