In =aiActivity.cs=, point the repo-level =.claude/commands= at the BISOS tree's =mother/_claude/commands=
when that tree exists on the platform, else at the resolved templates tree's own copy. =refresh=
re-evaluates it (so installing BISOS later is a =refresh=) and reports a dangling target. A sub does not
install it (inherited). Skills keep following their templates tree, as a whole. Interacts with
[[14.10]] (binding constants): add the new names there, not as new literals. Extend =verify.sh=:
homogeneous, heterogeneous, and no-BISOS scratch cases.
----- Results: ------
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented and tested 2026-10-19 (Mohsen confirmed dropping the activity-level commands override). Not
marked DONE: awaiting review.
- *=aiActivity.cs= (=py3/bin/=)*: new =bisosTemplatesTree= and two helpers, =_commandsSourceResolve= (the
  BISOS tree's =mother/_claude/commands= in its =/bisos/apps/...= spelling when that tree exists,
  else the
  resolved templates tree's own) and =_commandsLinkRefresh=. =initiate=: =commands= takes the resolved
  source; =settings.json= keeps the activity-over-mother preference. =refresh= calls the helper in base
  mode only; its description says so. The activity-level override for commands is dropped (no
  activity had
  one: =ls */_claude= showed =mother= only).
- *=_commandsLinkRefresh=*: missing, so created; a symlink to the right tree (compared resolved, so the
  =/bisos/apps= and =/bisos/git/...= spellings are one tree), so untouched; a symlink elsewhere or
  dangling, so replaced; a real directory, so never touched; skipped, with a note, when the
  templates have
  no commands directory or the project has no =.claude=.
- *Tested in scratch dirs*:
  - =initiate --activity=aiActivity --templates=<the fork>=: =.claude/commands= to the BISOS alias,
    while =settings.json= and =skills= follow the fork.
  - =refresh=: right link (OK, no change); link to the fork's commands (RETARGETED, pointed elsewhere);
    dangling (RETARGETED, dangling); a real directory (SKIP, untouched); missing (SYMLINKED, backfilled).
  - =initiateSub= creates no =.claude=, and =refresh= in the sub (MODE: sub) does not touch commands.
  - BISOS absent, by monkeypatching =bisosTemplatesTree= in a script: the fork's own commands are used;
    BISOS appearing later is picked up by one refresh; neither tree having commands, and no =.claude=,
    are skips.
