A CSXU (load =writing-cs-commands=, =comeega-authorship=, =dblock-authoring=, =bisos-pip-setup-py=):
=--base= (the templates base; inputs found by their fixed names), optionally =--workFlow= / =--de=
(paths: create the input symlinks). Verbs: assemble, check (dangling links, a path in both inputs,
missing inputs, links not in the manifest), and a dry run. Deep merge as in the design; relative links;
a manifest of what it made; never overwrites a real file; never commits. Logic in a pure module, as
=cmndsSync.py=; reuse its refusal style. Test in scratch trees (=verify.sh=), including a relative
=_skills= link and a collision.
----- Results: ------
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented and tested 2026-10-20. Not marked DONE: awaiting review. Nothing in a real base changed.
- *Files*: =py3/bin/aiActivityAssemble.cs= (new, =cs-mu=, verbs =assemblyDiff=, =assemblyCheck=,
  =assemblyUpdate= --- subject first; params =--base= (mandatory), =--workFlow=, =--de= (create the
  input links)); =py3/bisos/aiActivity/assemble.py= (new, =pyLibPure=); a =verify.sh= section; a README
  Key Files entry. Dblocks copied from =aiActivityCmnds.cs=, not regenerated in Blee.
- *Behaviour as designed*: deep merge (real directories; files as relative links through the input
  name, e.g. =mother/CLAUDE.md -> ../aiTemplates-workFlow/mother/CLAUDE.md=; input symlinks reproduced);
  a path in both inputs (or a leaf of one under a leaf of the other) refused; =__pycache__= and =.git=
  skipped. The manifest =.aiActivityAssembled= records each link /with its target/, so a link of ours
  changed by hand is a conflict, not silently replaced (a first version recorded paths only and failed
  that test). Removes links of ours no longer provided, then empty directories.
- *Against the real trees*: a scratch base with its two input links pointing at
  =/bxRepos/bxexamples/aiTemplates-{workFlow,DE}= assembled to 104 links, =IN SYNC= on check,
  idempotent; compared with the BISOS tree, every path resolves to byte-identical content, the two
  differences being =__pycache__/*.pyc= of a skill's =tools/= (skipped on purpose);
  =bisos-pip/_skills= and =aiActivity/_skills= list all 22 skills through the merged =mother/_skills=.
- *Migration preview for 18.5*: =assemblyDiff= on a copy of the BISOS tree with the two input links:
  100 conflicts (its real files) and 4 already the same (the three =_skills= links, =AI-Outputs.org=).
  So 18.5 removes the 100 provided paths first (git keeps them), then assembles.
- *Edge cases* (a script on synthetic trees, 16/16): missing input refused; merged skills through a
  relative activity link; the base's README untouched; relative links; idempotent; a relocated clone
  needs only its input link re-pointed; a rename removes the old link and adds the new; collision
  refused; a real file in the way and apply refusing without writing; a link of ours changed by hand;
  someone else's symlink; restoring after the way is cleared; the manifest's targets; an input link
  pointing elsewhere refused.
- *Not verified*: =verify.sh='s new section (not run: the package is not reinstalled, so the command is
  not on PATH); lint (no pyflakes); exit status is 0 for a refusal, as with =aiActivityCmnds.cs=.


