Found by =verify.sh= after 18.12: in a project initiated from the assembled base, =initiateSub=
failed with "Activity directory not found: .../bxexamples/aiTemplates-workFlow/xu-single", and a sub's
=refresh= read its files from =aiTemplates-workFlow/mother/= (=SKIP ... AI-Outputs.org=).
----- AI Results: ------
Fixed 2026-10-20. Not marked DONE: awaiting review. Nothing staged or committed.
- Cause: =_findInitiatedAncestor= fully resolved the parent's =AI-WORKFLOW.org= link. In an assembled
  base, =<base>/mother/AI-WORKFLOW.org= is itself a link into =aiTemplates-workFlow=, so the resolve
  ended in the input and the input became the base. =_deduceCwdConfig= did the same for relative links.
- Fix: a helper =_linkTargetOneHop(link)= (one hop: a relative target is joined to the link's directory
  and normalized, not resolved). Used by =_findInitiatedAncestor= (the base directory itself is then
  resolved, so =/bisos/apps/defaults/ai-templates= still compares equal to the bxexamples clone),
  =_deduceCwdConfig= (=AI-WORKFLOW.org= and =AI-Activity.org=) and =listClaudesPath='s display.
- Tested: a scratch project initiated from =/bisos/apps/defaults/ai-templates=, a =xu-single= sub ---
  installed, its =AI-Activity.org= points into the base, =refresh= reports =mode=sub=. =verify.sh= rc 0;
  the two failures are gone; the errors left are the expected cases (no parent, the assembler's
  refusals).
- Not tested: a heterogeneous sub against a fork's base. Tested 2026-10-20 (see 18.7, Re-tested): a
  BISOS =astro-site= sub under a project of the fork.


