Found in 18.7's skills change: the fork's DE turned an activity's =_skills/= (a real directory) into
=_skills -> ../mother/_skills=. The base still had the real directory the assembler had made for it,
holding only its own links, and =assemblyDiff= reported it as =CONFLICT (not ours, in the way)=.
----- AI Results: ------
Fixed 2026-10-20. Not marked DONE: awaiting review. Nothing staged or committed.
- =assemble.py= =planBuild=: the removals are computed first; a real directory in the way of a desired
  link is planned as a create when everything in it is a link of ours being removed (=planApply= already
  removes those, prunes the emptied directories, then links). Anything else in it --- a file, a foreign
  link --- keeps it a conflict, and nothing is written.
- Tested: the session's edge-case suite (=t18cases.py=), 18 earlier cases plus 5 new: the directory
  becomes the link and resolves to the merged skills, the base is then =IN SYNC=; with a foreign file
  inside, a conflict, apply refuses, the file is kept. 23/23. Then live on the fork's base (18.7).
- Not done: these cases are not in =verify.sh= (the suite lives in the session scratchpad).


